    isbefore: []  # e58a
    duplicate_of: []  # e58a
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e58a
    pr_ref:  # e58a
    description: "Discovered validating WI-razol (PR #4147). The WI-razol fix makes taint propagation honor ambiguous_names; it works, but the LIST is incomplete: 'copy' is not in python ambiguous_names, so 3 'python:external:0-0:copy:unresolved' edges still falsely match shutil.copy (host_fs) in the self-claims run. (os.environ.copy / ws_clients.copy / stdlib copy module are correctly suppressed by module mismatch; only truly-unresolved external 'copy' leaks.) Fix: add 'copy' to python ambiguous_names; better, audit per-language ambiguous_names for completeness against common-builtin collisions (copy, update, format, join, split, items, keys, values, ...) guided by which short names appear as external:unresolved in dogfood runs. Small residual (3 edges) -> P3, not a v6.0.0 blocker. Provenance: WI-razol end-to-end self-claims validation + behavior-map edge classification."  # e58a
    fields:  # e58a
      statement: "io_primitives/<lang>.yaml ambiguous_names must list every short name that is a catalog primitive method AND collides with a common non-IO builtin/method, so an unresolved bare call to that name is not falsely classified by either consumer (io-boundaries chain matcher or taint propagation)."  # e58a
      root_cause: "python ambiguous_names omits 'copy' (and likely peers), so 'python:external:0-0:copy:unresolved' edges falsely match the shutil.copy host_fs sink. The WI-razol matcher fix only suppresses names that ARE flagged ambiguous; completeness of the list is a separate catalog-data gap shared by both consumers."  # e58a
- op: discuss  # f5e1
  at: '2026-06-27T06:30:51Z'  # f5e1
  by: agent  # f5e1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f5e1
  clock: 2  # f5e1
  nonce: f5e1  # f5e1
  message: "io-boundary:F3 (PR #4324, dev c261dde7ab) does NOT close this. The kind-aware gate keys on IoPrimitive.kind; 'copy' is FUNCTION-kind (shutil.copy under functions:), so lookup_with_module('copy', None) still returns shutil.copy on a bare function-form call — the gate only suppresses 'copy' when the edge is an explicit method call (call_construct=method, i.e. x.copy()). So a bare external:copy edge that is a genuine method call on an untyped receiver is now suppressed, but a function-form bare copy() still matches. If the filed INV-mivud repro is method-form, F3 fixes it; if function-form, it persists and needs receiver typing (WI-fuvuj-class) or a module hint. Re-verify the filed repro's call_construct to decide; ambiguous_names remains the fallback. Status unchanged."  # f5e1
